<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:41Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>‘Fight through darkness, water’: Nepal survivor recounts escape from flood-hit tunnel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccc7922370362030023b46f17c3b4f15c5887b9bd06182d3d44548095e7ed085</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:21:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T17:22:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260903-fight-through-darkness-water-nepal-survivor-recounts-escape-from-flood-hit-tunnel--029aa5abd2d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260903-fight-through-darkness-water-nepal-survivor-recounts-escape-from-flood-hit-tunnel" /><summary type="html">A Nepalese worker recounts his harrowing escape from a hydropower project tunnel after last week's devastating flood. Around 900 workers remain trapped in tunnels at six hydroelectric plants in Nepal as the number of missing in the Himalayan disaster rose to 5,624 on Thursday, according to Nepalese and Chinese authorities.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Anti-Christian murder in Syria? No indication he was killed because of his faith</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38eb3596fe7025786ac960d1b86b0b44e84cf4f0d854f75e600b8a110328577d</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:21:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T17:00:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-anti-christian-murder-syria-no-indication-killed-faith--cf972620ce2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-anti-christian-murder-syria-no-indication-killed-faith" /><summary type="html">A Christian man by the name of Nader Boulos Tannous was murdered in Homs, Syria on August 15, 2026. After his death, Israel, Greece and Cyprus were quick to denounce what they called an anti-Christian act. Several days later however, authorities in Homs said the suspect had admitted killing Tannous as part of a personal dispute going back to 2012.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>WMO chief says El Nino could be strongest in four decades</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:658c5afd55c56eda14a34be8d43dae796b5125462de5ad1e6b940e6f033faf54</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T16:11:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-wmo-chief-says-el-nino-could-be-strongest-in-four-decades--061486528cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-wmo-chief-says-el-nino-could-be-strongest-in-four-decades" /><summary type="html">El Nino could be the strongest since records began four decades ago, the United Nations' climate agency warned Thursday, with the UN chief warning the world is in the "danger zone of extreme weather". The naturally-occurring weather phenomenon is set to become "very strong" in the months ahead and is near certain to persist through to February, the World Meteorological Organization (WMO) said. FRANCE 24's Journalist Carys Garland tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Two Palestinian teens killed in West Bank raid by Israeli settlers and army</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a34fe30a75d20113361d08532594f1b53b54cc5e237b17eea855d7bed0257978</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:21:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T16:09:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-two-palestinian-teens-killed-in-west-bank-raid-by-israeli-settlers-and-army--9187488fdbab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-two-palestinian-teens-killed-in-west-bank-raid-by-israeli-settlers-and-army" /><summary type="html">Two Palestinian teenagers ⁠were killed on ​Wednesday in an attack by Israeli settler militants and ​army troops on their village in the occupied West Bank, local officials and the Palestinian health ministry said, amid an uptick in violence ​by ‌Jewish settlers in the territory. The Israeli military said in a statement its forces had entered al-Mughayyir to ​provide security for police officers and an Israeli ‌civilian seeking to retrieve livestock.</summary></entry><entry><title>US energy firms dominate Venezuela deals worth billions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ec4d9d56936dbfd95c8e8e7796ee57000d09641fc672468c80fdb4cb4334317</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:21:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T16:06:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-us-energy-firms-dominate-venezuela-deals-worth-billions--d1c9283e2081.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-us-energy-firms-dominate-venezuela-deals-worth-billions" /><summary type="html">US energy firms on Wednesday signed a raft of multi-billion-dollar deals with Venezuela, days after the South American country agreed to grant the United States control of a huge chunk of its vast oil reserves. President Donald Trump has talked up the agreement on Venezuela's oil reserves as the "biggest oil deal in world history." But the deals have raised major questions about Venezuela's sovereignty, as FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>France agriculture production sees economic hit from heatwaves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e898af149e954bd9add039e176a098b7363a6eb84cf3eb2e6a94ab5ca0eba63d</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T16:05:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-agriculture-production-sees-economic-hit-from-heatwaves--a5510b56d96e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-agriculture-production-sees-economic-hit-from-heatwaves" /><summary type="html">France's recent heatwaves didn't just pose enormous health risks, they also hampered the economy. Authorities have estimated that the recent heat and drought caused production to plummet and expect wealth generated by the agricultural sector to decline by 8% over the course of the year. The knock-on effects will cost the French economy an estimated 0.1 percentage points of growth in 2026.</summary></entry><entry><title>US feminist icon and journalist Gloria Steinem dies aged 92</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:362299c42f7d15ae80cb26d32cb18cd49d51c87a8827f1355a0b54201f13876c</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:21:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:39:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-us-feminist-icon-and-journalist-gloria-steinem-dies-aged-92--49355b9195f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-us-feminist-icon-and-journalist-gloria-steinem-dies-aged-92" /><summary type="html">The co-founder of Ms. Magazine and celebrated feminist icon Gloria Steinem has died at her home at the age of 92. An internationally recognised activist in the fight for women's equality, she spoke out for the legalisation of abortion, same-sex marriage, and equal pay. She began her journalism career in New York in the 1960s. Politically, she was an outspoken critic of Donald Trump, arguing that the US had taken many steps back when it came to women's rights. FRANCE 24's Journalist and host of "The 51%" tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why Ukraine’s drained Kakhovka Dam is strategic for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b75535ba5b2e3b40864dc95cec2a68aaade9d7c558fdd5c1b4ac26f552fd4d2f</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:21:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:34:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-why-ukraine-drained-kakhovka-dam-strategic-russia--143f379d846d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-why-ukraine-drained-kakhovka-dam-strategic-russia" /><summary type="html">Small groups of Russian soldiers have been inching forward through the vast, drained Kakhovka reservoir since they blew up the dam in June 2023. Russian forces are infiltrating this “no man’s land” for reconnaissance purposes rather than for a future military offensive, said a military expert.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Giorgia Meloni government becomes Italy's longest-lasting since World War II</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb288a628352b3125b69aaa93eaaac4f7b7e219885bcbd67b44e4eb98525e145</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:21:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:29:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-giorgia-meloni-government-becomes-italy-s-longest-lasting-since-world-war-ii--f321ed0a24d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-giorgia-meloni-government-becomes-italy-s-longest-lasting-since-world-war-ii" /><summary type="html">Italy's first female Prime Minister, Giorgia Meloni, has surpassed a longevity record set by the late Silvio Berlusconi. When she took office in 2022, many European allies viewed her with unease, given her party's neo-fascist roots. Yet she has governed pragmatically, working within EU institutions and even supporting Ukraine. Domestically, however, she has targeted same-sex parents and clamped down on press freedom.</summary></entry><entry><title>France-UK ties and humour celebrated as London receives Bayeux Tapestry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4f28fcafbce4d727dccf31cadd35d6f3c5887ff42527d509fd46f5f395c28cb</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:21:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:27:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-uk-ties-and-humour-celebrated-as-london-receives-bayeux-tapestry-1--6ef2090555dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-uk-ties-and-humour-celebrated-as-london-receives-bayeux-tapestry-1" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel #Macron is in #London on the occasion of the #Bayeux Tapestry's exhibition at the #BritishMuseum. The 1,000-year-old work of woven art recounts the Battle of #Hastings, in which William the Conqueror – #KingCharles's ancestor – led the Norman Conquest of #England. An opportunity for the French president, the British PM Andy #Burnham and British monarch to celebrate the strong ties between the two countries.</summary></entry><entry><title>Driverless robotaxis hit the streets of London</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efec253a90027fce096ebcfe9e41caa1552e9e6bfec4d3ff4989f16ae79cbe21</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:16:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-driverless-robotaxis-hit-the-streets-of-london--2660dfa1427c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-driverless-robotaxis-hit-the-streets-of-london" /><summary type="html">London is entering the era of autonomous vehicles: driverless cabs are now available through Uber and British tech firm Wayve in the capital. It marks a setback for Google's Waymo and Chinese giant Baidu, which have been eyeing Europe as a largely untapped market for autonomous vehicles. But for Wayve, it is its first mass-market rollout, and the company now plans to expand to Tokyo and 10 other cities with Uber.</summary></entry><entry><title>Murder of Daphne Caruana Galizia: Campaigner 'devastated' at tycoon's acquittal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afe1f013db35ec073f82243c21cac55cba688bcc63c3eff339ddab8709175ad5</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/i-m-devastated-by-the-verdict-says-tom-gibson-deputy-dir-for-committee-to-protect-journalists--f0de620fc0ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/i-m-devastated-by-the-verdict-says-tom-gibson-deputy-dir-for-committee-to-protect-journalists" /><summary type="html">A campaigner who has worked on the case of murdered Maltese journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia since she was killed by a car bomb in 2017 has spoken of his devastation at the not guilty verdict.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish PM Sanchez says no evidence Morocco orchestrated Ceuta border surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8380608a428d22b40240e0246814f5517989a3fc980959047e6e9d72b54f7e28</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:10:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-evidence-morocco-orchestrated-ceuta-border-surge--2deeeb297365.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-evidence-morocco-orchestrated-ceuta-border-surge" /><summary type="html">Spain has found no evidence to conclude that July's deadly border rush from Morocco into its enclave of Ceuta was orchestrated by Moroccan authorities, ​Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez ‌said on Thursday, countering allegations in a Spanish police report. Speaking in parliament, Sanchez responded to claims in ⁠the report that emerged this week suggesting the entry of over 70,000 people into Ceuta was not a spontaneous migration but a planned effort to overwhelm  border controls.</summary></entry><entry><title>Outrage mounts in Malta after acquittal over journalist's murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:718bdeed0a2a2abc47a059780a4087ff1c2a1966c6b815654622dac939daee56</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:07:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-outrage-mounts-in-malta-after-acquittal-over-journalist-s-murder--d56805968908.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-outrage-mounts-in-malta-after-acquittal-over-journalist-s-murder" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of people demonstrated in the Maltese capital Valletta after a wealthy businessman was found not guilty of masterminding the murder of an investigative journalist. The verdict on Daphne Caruana Galizia's car-bomb killing in 2017 sparked outrage from Maltese civil society groups and international media freedom organisations. The opposition Nationalist Party, which organised the demonstration late on Wednesday, has said lawmakers should be called back from their summer break for a special session of the legislature to discuss the case.</summary></entry><entry><title>Beastie Boy Mike D releases his first solo LP 'Thank You'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b20d4c2072d4926a46e11174fd7a61fb257d6ab0ea1c8ed4b3eac97eb0b3a1d</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T14:51:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260903-beastie-boy-mike-d-releases-his-first-solo-lp-thank-you--f6e4724b54c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260903-beastie-boy-mike-d-releases-his-first-solo-lp-thank-you" /><summary type="html">Mike D rose to fame in the 1980s as part of New York's Beastie Boys, a rap-rock trio who soon tired of poking fun at frat boy humour with hits like "Fight for Your Right (To Party!)" and" Girls". The band quickly moved on thanks to their passion for beat making, sampling and playing around in the studio, establishing themselves over three decades as credible genre-bending musicians.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>'Glacier melt and sea level rise will continue:  We cannot leave this to the next generation'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10fabac2db8cbda9f0ac69a091bd0f77c344f11785c96cc942b11c2317974660</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T14:45:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-glacier-melt-and-sea-level-rise-will-continue-we-cannot-leave-this-to-the-next-generation--98482303a44a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-glacier-melt-and-sea-level-rise-will-continue-we-cannot-leave-this-to-the-next-generation" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Inger Andersen, Under-Secretary-General of the United Nations and Executive Director of the United Nations Environment Programme. Her central argument is that decades of what she calls “carbon procrastination” have made exceeding 1.5°C unavoidable: the question is therefore no longer simply whether the world crosses 1.5°C, but by how much, for how long, and with what consequences for vulnerable societies and ecosystems. While mitigation remains essential, adaptation becomes equally important as sea-level rise and glacier loss, will continue even as emissions fall.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal Floods: Survivors hauled to safety with makeshift zip line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0daa8faf9a6af0a9df2890621c286ab1870cab02e6bfadaad708feaf466b654</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T14:43:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-nepal-floods-survivors-hauled-to-safety-with-makeshift-zip-line--9e6818333ecc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-nepal-floods-survivors-hauled-to-safety-with-makeshift-zip-line" /><summary type="html">Nepali authorities have erected a makeshift zip line to help stranded residents travel across the swollen waters of the Trishuli river after last week’s deadly flash floods swept away bridges, leaving them cut off from the outside world. Some were in need of urgent treatment, medicines, food and other essentials.</summary></entry><entry><title>Please welcome the newest member to our team: The AI agent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69cfa1c5ea792d1147adac17dbe8aff4432c3401b796a2e42cad5742c997fd1b</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T14:25:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20260903-please-welcome-the-newest-member-to-our-team-the-ai-agent--5d0b8850eed6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20260903-please-welcome-the-newest-member-to-our-team-the-ai-agent" /><summary type="html">This week, we're looking look at efforts to incorporate artificial intelligence into the workplace. But not just your run-of-the-mill generative AI chatbot: we're focusing on actual AI agents. These are autonomous programs designed to take on tasks and work through a series of steps without the user having to specify every move. And they're moving into our everyday lives – helping people plan holidays, shop online and take care of other routine tasks.</summary><category term="People &amp; Profit" /></entry><entry><title>A 'Lille' bit of everything at Europe's biggest flea market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b702630fe356293387b28206d4a72970cb026dd5084e9a856c2f6d7a6fda9209</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T14:00:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260903-a-lille-bit-of-everything-at-europe-s-biggest-flea-market--63ea454215c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260903-a-lille-bit-of-everything-at-europe-s-biggest-flea-market" /><summary type="html">Every year, millions of people flock to the French city of Lille on the first weekend of September for Europe's biggest flea market, the "Braderie de Lille". We dive into its rich history, the many terms for second-hand shopping in French, plus the delicious tradition that's now synonymous with this 34-hour event: mussels and fries!</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Tunisia water crisis deepens as temperatures approach 50°C</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75e91d7604927cf52f3a702a254d845c1c71ea94635f20680f77b18a915b8cb6</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T13:52:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-tunisia-water-crisis-deepens-as-temperatures-approach-50_c--25ad983d7cc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-tunisia-water-crisis-deepens-as-temperatures-approach-50%C2%B0c" /><summary type="html">In Tunisia, powerful heatwaves are driving power cuts and water shortage. While the country has been dealing with structural water scarcity and recurring drought for years, the current crisis is fuelling anger against the government, even as authorities attempt to coordinate water distribution efforts to quell the crisis.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's Macron meets UK PM Burnham at Downing Street</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc3b8d3c94278d0f0446aed7dd67310eaa73ab74c93ce36700bded64075b3594</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T13:45:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-s-macron-meets-uk-pm-burnham-at-downing-street--e3b95d5ceaa7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-s-macron-meets-uk-pm-burnham-at-downing-street" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron met Britain’s new Prime Minister, Andy Burnham, for official talks at 10 Downing Street. The meeting came a day after the pair were joined by King Charles and Queen Camilla at the British Museum for a preview of the Bayeux Tapestry exhibition in London. Macron is the first EU leader to meet Burnham. Talks are expected to cover relations between Britain and the European Union, support for Ukraine, and migrant crossings in the English Channel.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli attacks in West Bank at 'unprecedented' level, PNI leader Barghouti says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c033ea81cfe509393d7a6a68bf5b43387f7a5b4ce03ca6c11cc6ebb800fa38d7</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T13:26:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260903-israeli-attacks-in-west-bank-at-unprecedented-level-pni-leader-barghouti-says--38c73f0a94fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260903-israeli-attacks-in-west-bank-at-unprecedented-level-pni-leader-barghouti-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, the secretary general of the Palestinian National Initiative (PNI) party Mustafa Barghouti said the level of Israeli attacks on Palestinians in the West Bank had become "totally unprecedented". With tensions escalating, activists accuse settlers of operating with total impunity. "Their goal is clear: it is ethnic cleansing," Barghouti stated, calling Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's reaction to the attacks hypocritical.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Ceuta crisis: ‘No evidence Morocco behind border surge’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41bb8cdca1b5cdf6533a73685b29d328559953c8df1f0465fbba15a8d8060301</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T13:05:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-ceuta-crisis-no-evidence-morocco-behind-border-surge-1--99ca84dd5d77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-ceuta-crisis-no-evidence-morocco-behind-border-surge-1" /><summary type="html">There is no evidence Morocco was behind the mass influx of migrants that overwhelmed the Spanish enclave of Ceuta in July, Spanish PM Pedro Sanchez told lawmakers Thursday. Sanchez's comments followed a police report that emerged this week saying that the mass entry into Ceuta was not a spontaneous migration event but a planned and phased operation designed to overwhelm border controls.</summary></entry><entry><title>France recorded 'hottest summer ever' in 2026, environment minister says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b555f89a31c4ed3b7463b1592b3ee6681aeaef2e6f8db2645a204cfc65e72044</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T12:47:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260903-france-recorded-hottest-summer-ever-in-2026-environment-minister-says--331c447a1dc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260903-france-recorded-hottest-summer-ever-in-2026-environment-minister-says" /><summary type="html">The summer of 2026 was the hottest summer ever recorded since measurements began in 1990, French Environment Minister Monique Barbut said Thursday.</summary><category term="France" /></entry></feed>
